{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-97469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $X∼B(7,0.7),$ compute $P(X=5).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(7,0.7),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.7)^{x}(0.3)^{7-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =f(5) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{5})(0.7)^{5}(0.3)^{7-5} \\\\  & =21(0.7)^{5}(0.3)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.3177\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-97469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value