ory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-96728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-96728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.0256"] ["math" "0.0521"] ["math" "0.0825"] ["math" "0.1028"] ["math" "0.1274"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-96728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.0256"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $X∼B(6,0.8),$ compute $P(X=4).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(6,0.8),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{x})(0.8)^{x}(0.2)^{6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4})(0.8)^{4}(0.2)^{6-4} \\\\  & =15(0.8)^{4}(0.2)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.2458\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-97468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.1554"] ["math" "0.2458"] ["math" "0.2989"] ["math" "0.3011"] ["math" "0.3446"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.2458"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $X∼B(6,0.6),$ compute $P(X=3).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(6,0.6),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{x})(0.6)^{x}(0.4)^{6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3})(0.6)^{3}(0.4)^{6-3} \\\\  & =20(0.6)^{3}(0.4)^{3} \\\\  & ≈0.2765\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-97464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.1792"] ["math" "0.2443"] ["math" "0.2765"] ["math" "0.3208"] ["math" "0.3557"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.2765"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $X∼B(7,0.3),$ then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(X=1)≈${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial, we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(7,0.3),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x}){(0.3)}^{x}{(0.7)}^{7-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1) & =f(1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{1}){(0.3)}^{1}{(0.7)}^{7-1} \\\\  & =7{(0.3)}^{1}{(0.7)}^{6} \\\\  & ≈0.247\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-279626" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279626" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.247"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-129971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $X∼B(4,\\frac{1}{3}),$ compute $P(X<3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-129971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(4,\\frac{1}{3}),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{x}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-2} \\\\  & =1{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4}+4{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{3}+6{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-129971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-129971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-129971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{81}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{243}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{81}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-129971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $X∼B(3,\\frac{3}{4}),$ then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(X<2)≈${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial, we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(3,\\frac{3}{4}),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{x}){(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & =P(X\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}){(\\frac{3}{4})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}){(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-1} \\\\  & =1{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}+3{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.156\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-279689" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279689" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.156"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $X∼B(6,0.2),$ compute $P(X>4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(6,0.2),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{x})(0.2)^{x}(0.8)^{6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =P(X\\in {5,6}) \\\\  & =f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})(0.2)^{5}(0.8)^{6-5}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{6})(0.2)^{6}(0.8)^{6-6} \\\\  & =6(0.2)^{5}(0.8)+1(0.2)^{6}(0.8)^{0} \\\\  & =0.0016.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-97510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256"