rac{2}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5}+5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4}+10{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3} \\\\  & ≈0.210\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-279694" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-279694" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.210"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $X∼B(3,0.3),$ compute $P(X\\ge 2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(3,0.3),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{x})(0.3)^{x}(0.7)^{3-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X\\in {2,3}) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})(0.3)^{2}(0.7)^{3-2}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3})(0.3)^{3}(0.7)^{3-3} \\\\  & =3(0.3)^{2}(0.7)+1(0.3)^{3}(0.7)^{0} \\\\  & =0.216.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb005120cea2be0499d5eaa05b3b89efd56836d2e3b8ccaa7a5b9679bac0fd21"} {"question" "q-97503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.154"] ["math" "0.189"] ["math" "0.216"] ["math" "0.227"] ["math" "0.273"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7f8a2de868752a93d7cbfd"} {"question" "q-97503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.216"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069463/state.json" "file_sha256" "be737d4a4ca1e1de45387dc36174cf8d0bfe6795fc7